# === Punt Labs canonical .gitignore ===
# Source of truth: .bin/gitignore-canonical.template
# Rollout:         .bin/gitignore-canonical-rollout.sh
# Repo-specific additions belong BELOW the "# === Repo-specific ===" marker.
# Everything above it is managed by the rollout script.

# --- Secrets & local overrides ---
.env
.env.*
.env*.local
!.env.example
.envrc.local
.biff.local
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.*
.claude/mcp.local.json
.mcp.local.json
*.local
*.local.*
.*.local
.*.local.*

# --- Punt Labs runtime state (never commit) ---
.punt-labs/local/
.punt-labs/**/local/**
.punt-labs/**/*.local.*
.punt-labs/quarry/captures/
.punt-labs/vox/ephemeral/
.punt-labs/vox/vox.local.md
.punt-labs/lux.md

# --- Claude Code runtime state ---
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
.claude/scheduled_tasks*
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/projects/
.claude/beadle.poll.t
*/**/.claude/

# --- Lock files (except uv.lock) ---
.*.lock
*.punt-import.lock
.CLAUDE.md.lock
.CLAUDE.md.punt-import.lock
**/.create.lock

# --- Beads runtime state ---
.beads/bd.sock*
.beads/beads.db*
.beads/daemon-*
.beads/daemon.log
.beads/daemon-error
.beads/.local_version

# --- Scratch / temp ---
.tmp/*
!.tmp/.gitkeep
*.tmp
CLAUDE.md.tmp

# --- Worktrees ---
.worktrees/

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashe
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
.codex/
.accio/
.claude-flow/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.mypy_cache/
.pyright/
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-work/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
uv.toml

# --- Node / web ---
node_modules/
.astro/
.vercel/

# --- Go ---
coverage.out
*.test

# --- Swift / Xcode ---
# (Do NOT ignore *.xcodeproj / *.xcworkspace — those directories are tracked;
# only ignore user-specific state INSIDE them.)
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
CoverageDerived/
*.xccheckout
*.xcresult
*.xcscmblueprint
*.hmap
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip
*.ipa
.swiftpm/
Package.pin
Package.resolved
Carthage/Build/
Carthage/Checkout
Pods/
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output
iOSInjectionProject/
playground.xcworkspace
timeline.xctimeline

# --- LaTeX build artifacts ---
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fl
*.log
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# === Repo-specific ===

# Scratch directory (TMPDIR set via .envrc)

# Plugin-generated per-repo state. Claude Code clones this repo onto every
# user's machine when they run `claude plugin marketplace add`, so anything
# tracked here ships to all consumers. A submodule tracked here is worse than
# leakage — it breaks the install outright (see CLAUDE.md, "Why This Repo Is
# Different"). Keep these on disk for local tooling; never commit them.
.vox/
.lux/
.biff
.beads/

# Same leak, narrower paths — these sit beside files the repo legitimately
# tracks, so they are named individually. Ignoring all of `.claude/` or all of
# `.github/workflows/` would mask real content: `.github/workflows/docs.yml`
# is this repo's only CI.
#   settings.json  — written by `vox enable` and punt-kit init; registers hooks
#                    by absolute path to one machine's plugin install, so it is
#                    inert-to-broken on anyone else's disk.
#   biff-notify.yml — written by `biff enable`; posts session events to the
#                    team's NATS relay, and would run in every consumer's fork
#                    against credentials they do not have.
#
# `.claude/hooks/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Every occupant observed across
# the org — check-branch.sh, no-push-to-main.sh, make-check-gate.sh — is
# portable governance shell, and koch-trainer-swift tracks its copies on
# purpose. Ignoring the directory would silently block this repo from
# committing a repo-authored validation hook, and silently is the operative
# word: `git add` skips an ignored path without a word, so the author gets no
# signal at all. The machine-specific occupant is settings.json, and that is
# what is named.
.github/workflows/biff-notify.yml

# A submodule here does not leak data, it breaks the install: Claude Code
# clones this repo with submodules, so an SSH submodule URL aborts the clone
# for every user without a GitHub SSH key.
#
# `.gitmodules` is deliberately NOT ignored, and this comment exists so nobody
# re-adds it. Ignoring it hid the file twice over: `git status` went quiet
# locally, and CI could not see it either, because a checkout materialises only
# tracked files. It also bought nothing — `git submodule add` stages
# .gitmodules with --force regardless of any ignore rule (verified). Leaving it
# visible restores the local signal at no cost, because the leak-guard job in
# .github/workflows/docs.yml fails the build on both the file and the gitlink
# (mode 160000).

# The lux display process writes ImGui window geometry into its working
# directory on exit. Per-machine screen state (pane sizes, docking layout) that
# would follow a consumer's window manager around. Named exactly rather than
# `*.ini`: an unanchored `*.ini` matches at any depth and would silently
# swallow a future tox.ini, pytest.ini, or mypy.ini, and `git add` skips an
# ignored path without a word. Every .ini observed across the org's repos is
# one of these three shapes.
imgui.ini
Lux.ini
Lux_*.ini

# The mandated sibling lock every punt CLI takes before mutating a shared
# host file (tool-enable-disable.md 2.4). Per-machine runtime state, and it
# persists by design — unlinking a lock file races the next writer. The
# pattern is broad because the lock's name is the host file's, and tools
# differ on the suffix — .CLAUDE.md.lock and .CLAUDE.md.punt-import.lock
# both appear.
.*.lock
